module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.SheafCohomology.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.CechNerveHomology
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Totally acyclic abelian sheaves

Let `(C, J)` be a site. An abelian sheaf `F` on it is *totally acyclic* when its cohomology
over every sheaf of sets vanishes in every positive degree. This is Stacks 072Y, the
hypothesis under which Čech cohomology computes sheaf cohomology for an arbitrary covering.

Cohomology over a sheaf of sets `K` is defined here as `Ext` from the free abelian sheaf
generated by `K` to `F`: the free abelian sheaf functor is left adjoint to taking the
underlying presheaf of sets, so the free abelian sheaf on `K` represents the functor of
sections over `K`, and `Ext` from it is therefore the derived functor of those sections.
This is the definition the source makes, read through that adjunction.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Cohomology.cohomologyOverSheaf`: the degree-`p` cohomology of an abelian sheaf
  over a sheaf of sets.
* `Stacks.Cohomology.IsTotallyAcyclic`: vanishing of all those groups in positive degrees.

## Implementation notes

The free abelian sheaf is `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf` applied to the
underlying presheaf of sets of `K`; no second copy of that construction is made here.
Vanishing of an abelian group is expressed as `Subsingleton` of its underlying type, which
avoids having to produce a zero object in the universe `w'` of the `Ext`-groups and is what
the consumers of the condition use.

The universe `w'` of the `Ext`-groups is independent of the universe `w` of the sheaves, as
it is for Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.H`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 072Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/072Y)
* [SGA 4], Exposé Vbis, Proposition 1.3.10
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe w' w v u

open CategoryTheory

namespace Stacks.Cohomology

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasExt.{w'} (Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w})]

/-- The degree-`p` cohomology of an abelian sheaf `F` over a sheaf of sets `K`, namely the
`p`-th `Ext`-group from the free abelian sheaf generated by `K` to `F`. -/
abbrev cohomologyOverSheaf (K : Sheaf J (Type w)) (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}) (p : ℕ) :
    Type w' :=
  Abelian.Ext ((Presheaf.freeAbelianSheaf J).obj K.obj) F p

/-- An abelian sheaf is **totally acyclic** if its cohomology over every sheaf of sets
vanishes in every positive degree. -/
@[stacks 072Y, sga "4 V 4.1" "flasque case"]
def IsTotallyAcyclic (F : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}) : Prop :=
  ∀ (K : Sheaf J (Type w)) (p : ℕ), 1 ≤ p → Subsingleton (cohomologyOverSheaf J K F p)

end Stacks.Cohomology
